Subject: Tweak: training
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

The Strikers 101 lessons take players off the field with their own
challenge setting, awaymissingsidekicks (and its home twin): at every
kickoff cTeam::ResetCharacters puts that many fielders of the team in
FROZEN_SHATTERED, the state Crystal Canyon's solar flares vaporize players
with. They are intangible and invisible, and the AI and the pad switch pass
them over. With 4 the captain goes too (the first lesson's Mario team);
the goalie always stays.

The launcher's Start training (or --training) goes into a training match: it
passes the title at once, as Skip intro does, and the title's handler goes
on into the match instead of the main menu, as the demo match starts from
the title (which stays under the loading). The main menu reads the game
save otherwise, so the title reads it first and starts the match once it
is in: Domination with the host's captain and stadium, both captains'
sidekicks from the save's lineups (mRulesTable, the Teams page's), its
match settings, and the pad that passed the title on the home side. The
away captain is Bowser, or Mario against Bowser. g_bTrainingMatch marks
the match; GameInfoManager::SetMode, which the menus call for every other
match, clears it, so no other match changes.

In that match, the team nobody plays loses its four fielders at every
kickoff, and its goalie stays in goal. The team that trains starts every
kickoff with the host's item (one of it, cGame::ResetPowerups, after the
game emptied the slots) and keeps every item it uses: DesireUsePowerup no
longer clears it once thrown. The match is a single one to 10 goals
(SetupGameFromConfig, on this match's own settings copy, which nothing
saves) that never ends on them: the goal checks of cGame::CheckForGoal and
FinishMegaStrike, the end of match presentations they would call
(Presentation), the goal overlay's winner caption and Match point pass it
over. It ends from the pause menu, into the main menu.

